  "honest_assessment": "Core 2.5D perception (spatial hash insertion + Nav2 costmap rasterization) achieved a warm mean of 121.986 ms (8.2 FPS) and median p50 of 57.899 ms (17.27 FPS). While median latency (57.899 ms / 17.27 FPS) meets 10 Hz, the warm mean was 121.986 ms due to CPU thermal throttling under back-to-back sequential execution. Optimization achieved 22.2x speedup on spatial hash insertion (53.311 ms vs baseline 1185.84 ms) and 41.7x speedup on costmap rasterization (68.675 ms vs baseline 2863.59 ms). Dual-rate asynchronous decoupling enables the Fast Path to run at 21.93 FPS (mean 45.603 ms, p50 48.814 ms) with concurrent background SalsaNext inference (~3106.967 ms mean). Sequential CPU inference alone operates at 0.31 FPS warm."
